menu "Michi Music Stream Audio"

    config MICHI_AUDIO_RING_BUFFER_KB
        int "Audio ring buffer size (KiB, allocated in PSRAM)"
        default 1024
        range 16 16384
        help
          Size of the SPSC ring between the network/session producer and the
          I2S consumer task. Default 1024 = 1 MB in PSRAM. The 4 MB legacy
          ring (unsynchronized, static) was replaced: 1 MB at 48 kHz/16-bit
          stereo holds ~5.5 s, plenty for network jitter at the current
          validation baseline. Larger values increase jitter tolerance at
          the cost of PSRAM. Changes take effect on the next session start.
          A ring_buffer_kb of 0 in michi_audio_output_config_t selects this
          default (the option is used when the config is 0). The size must
          be a power of two (16..16384 KiB): the ring indices are masked.

endmenu
